<!--
  Mary Had a Little Lamb
  Traditional American tune, words by Sarah Josepha Hale (1830). Public domain.
  C major, 4/4, quarter = 100, 16 bars: two verses (38 s). Right hand: the melody, C4-G4.
  Left hand: C3 and G3, one per bar. Every note is in C3-B4.

  bar | right hand  | left hand | words
    1 | E4 D4 C4 D4 | C3        | Ma-ry had a
    2 | E4 E4 E4    | C3        | lit-tle lamb,
    3 | D4 D4 D4    | G3        | lit-tle lamb,
    4 | E4 G4 G4    | C3        | lit-tle lamb,
    5 | E4 D4 C4 D4 | C3        | Ma-ry had a
    6 | E4 E4 E4 E4 | C3        | lit-tle lamb, its
    7 | D4 D4 E4 D4 | G3        | fleece was white as
    8 | C4          | C3        | snow.
    9 | E4 D4 C4 D4 | C3        | Ev-ery-where that
   10 | E4 E4 E4    | C3        | Ma-ry went,
   11 | D4 D4 D4    | G3        | Ma-ry went,
   12 | E4 G4 G4    | C3        | Ma-ry went,
   13 | E4 D4 C4 D4 | C3        | ev-ery-where that
   14 | E4 E4 E4 E4 | C3        | Ma-ry went, the
   15 | D4 D4 E4 D4 | G3        | lamb was sure to
   16 | C4          | C3        | go.
-->
